fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: glassback_bull
name: Glassback Bull
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  # v0.3: Boss, durability 6, attack +3, light armor, rating 13.
  level: 3
  role: boss
  armor: 1
  morale: 6
  weapon: A rack wider than a cart
  wants: Distance, the clearing, and the herd behind it.
  special: 'RINGING CHARGE — it charges in a straight line and cannot turn inside the charge:
    anyone who commits to stepping aside instead of meeting it is not in the path. When it
    closes from a distance its antlers ring, and at the end of the next exchange the MM may
    bring one Glassback Cow to the edge of the scene.'
  when_bloodied: The season goes out of it. It stops charging, turns broadside and backs toward
    the herd. It still answers anyone who closes, but it has stopped starting anything.
  tells: Nine feet at the shoulder and a small sunrise on its head, pawing a straight line
    in the turf toward the largest thing in the clearing.
  breaks: Walks, not runs, back to the herd. Nothing in this book is less interested in finishing
    a fight.
  twists:
  - It is out of season and entirely avoidable, and someone in the party wants the antlers
    anyway.
  - It has already shed one side of its rack, and it is lopsided and furious about it.
  - 'A hunter has wounded it: it starts the fight already bloodied.'
  - The clearing is narrow, with trees on both sides, and stepping aside is Hard.
  - Another bull is contesting the herd, and the party has walked into the middle of it.
  - It has picked the largest, most armoured party member, and nothing else exists for it.
  nastier: The charge rings every time it closes, and a cow arrives at the end of every exchange
    it rings.
  description: >-
    Nine feet at the shoulder in season, and the rack is wider than a cart. The mineral has
    gone milky with age at the base and stayed clear at the tips, so that a bull in low sun
    looks like it is carrying a small sunrise on its head. It is not aggressive for eleven
    months of the year.
  notes: >-
    Level 3 Boss, armor 1: no overrides. The entry-tier Boss, and one the party can decline:
    every step backwards buys real ground, and a party that gives it the clearing gets to
    keep everything else, including any antler already shed.


    In season, and therefore not reasonable. Out of season it is the single most avoidable
    danger in this book. Its first target is the largest thing in the clearing: armour makes
    you a candidate, and standing still does not save you. Its bloodied phase is written to
    be reached by withdrawing as much as by winning.


    Appears: one bull per herd, and only dangerous in the eight weeks of season.
  reskin_of: null
